{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDFQnQNcxk1d1mu4b5DW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I judged this function **not vulnerable** and wrote that to `results/s203.json`, with `cwe` set to null and no vulnerable statements.\n\nThe function `remove_device_compression_modes` (from the Intel IAA crypto driver) goes through each of the device's compression-mode slots:\n- **Empty slots:** it skips them, so nothing is used if it isn't there.\n- **Filled slots:** it runs the mode's own cleanup function if one exists, then frees the device's copy of the mode once.\n- **After freeing:** it sets the slot to NULL, so calling this function again can't free the same memory twice or use it after it's freed.\n\nOne thing I couldn't check from this file alone: line 11 reads `iaa_compression_modes[i]->free` without first checking that `iaa_compression_modes[i]` exists. It's safe as long as the shared mode table entry is still there whenever a device holds that mode. The code that keeps those in step is in other files, so I assumed it rather than verified it. I mentioned adding a NULL check there as optional hardening in the `suggested_fix` field, not as a vulnerability."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_read_input_tokens":22105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8e288ba-32bf-4a2c-90ca-9f7bcd73bff9","uuid":"8368130d-787f-49f2-aed6-06043ba9d799","timestamp":"2026-11-20T00:40:31.557Z","request_id":"req_011ChDFQnGCRRe3RPkA1g8aY"}
